<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 293 0 R/Alt(Three shaded views of a CAD model. Left: a rectangular box of square aluminum tubes with two long rails and cross members in each of the top and bottom frames joined by four corner posts; three dark blocks are lumped masses, three short tubes carry small blocks marked with orange triangles, open black squares mark the four mount points, and an orange star marks a small orange block on a gray bracket at one top corner, the hardening member. Middle: a close-up of that member: an orange rectangular mass spans two thin red-brown strips whose ends are clamped on a gray steel bracket that stands on a chassis tube; text labels name the tuned mass, the two thin strips, the steel bracket and the chassis tube. Right: the article hanging on four thin cords, with six blue cylindrical shakers, each with a black arrow showing its force direction; blue filled circles mark control gauge points, open orange diamonds mark held-out gauge points and orange triangles mark the tip gauges, the member's mid-span included.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[18]/Pg 877 0 R>>
