<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 316 0 R/Alt(Three panels. (a) Tone frequency on a log scale from 20 to 2000 Hz against time from 0 to about 400 s: a solid blue straight line rising from 20 Hz at 0 s to 2000 Hz at about 399 s (T1); a dashed orange line rising over about 100 s (T2); a dash-dot green line falling from 2000 Hz to 20 Hz over about 399 s (T5); a dotted purple staircase rising over about 150 s (T3); and a short thick red segment at about 74 Hz over 10 s (T4). (b) Reference over specification in dB against frequency from 20 to 2000 Hz: the median control near 0 dB at 20 Hz, falling to between about minus 2 and minus 20 dB above 60 Hz; the lowest control dotted, often between minus 20 and minus 50 dB; a shaded range up to a few dB over 0. (c) Engine volts from 0 to 2.3 against frequency: the largest ideal drive is 1 V at 20 Hz, falls to about 0.5 V by 100 Hz and to under 0.3 V above 300 Hz; a dashed line at 1 V and a dash-dot line at 2 V mark the peak and the ceiling.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[28]/Pg 878 0 R>>
