<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 473 0 R/Alt((a) Three bars, each 100 percent of its claims, split into holds, weaker and does not hold. Law differences, 436 claims: 78 percent hold, 19 percent hold weaker and 3 percent do not hold. Levels, 1,895 claims: 82, 16 and 2 percent. Effects of the structure, 213 claims: 89, 10 and 1 percent. (b) A scatter with a dashed diagonal of equality. The IEC share and completion points lie below zero on both axes, the worst over-test points above zero on both, and most lie near the diagonal, with most quartile bars crossing it. The two effects that do not hold are a completion square at zero on the held-back axis, well left of the diagonal, and an IEC share circle just below zero on the held-back axis.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[31]/Pg 885 0 R>>
